{"ts": 0.100484, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;97m4.2 — the pipe\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nA \u001b[36mpipe\u001b[0m ( \u001b[92m|\u001b[0m ) sends the standard output of one\r\ncommand into the standard input of the next. \u001b[91mMost important idea\r\nin the shell.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[92mwc\u001b[0m alone counts:\r\n  \u001b[92mwc -l poem.txt\u001b[0m          \u001b[90m# lines in poem.txt\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[92mwc\u001b[0m via pipe counts \u001b[36mwhatever you piped in\u001b[0m:\r\n  \u001b[92mseq 1 100 | wc -l\u001b[0m       \u001b[90m# 100\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[92mls /usr/bin | wc -l\u001b[0m     \u001b[90m# how many programs are installed\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nPipes stack:\r\n  \u001b[92mls /usr/bin | sort | head\u001b[0m        \u001b[90m# list → sort → first 10\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[92mls /usr/bin | grep ^a\u001b[0m            \u001b[90m# names starting with 'a'\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[92mls /usr/bin | grep ^a | wc -l\u001b[0m    \u001b[90m# …and count them\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nThings to notice while you try these:\r\n  - \u001b[92m|\u001b[0m is Shift+Backslash on most keyboards.\r\n  - Each piece is a normal command; only the connector is new.\r\n  - The pipeline runs left-to-right; output flows.\r\n\r\n\u001b[93m▶ Try a few pipelines, then \u001b[92mnext\u001b[93m.\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 995}
