{"ts": 0.278736, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;97mSTAGE 5 — Ready for vimtutor\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nFour lessons, then a gate. By the end, you'll know the difference\r\nbetween a command that prints-and-exits and one that takes over the\r\nterminal; you'll be able to leave any of them deliberately; and you'll\r\nunderstand why Vim has \u001b[92m:w\u001b[0m, \u001b[92m:q\u001b[0m, and \u001b[92m:q!\u001b[0m.\r\n\r\nAfter the gate, this tutor hands you to \u001b[92mvimtutor\u001b[0m (if it's\r\ninstalled on your system) — that is the next step.\r\n\r\n\u001b[93m▶ Type \u001b[92mnext\u001b[93m to begin lesson 5.1.\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 502}
{"ts": 0.279156, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 251}
